ROLE
You are adding a unified console/logging helper to the mfaw Python CLI so its
terminal output matches the look of the GHL Agentic Workspace CLI (Clack-styled:
vertical bar on the left, intro/outro framing, smooth spinners, color-coded
log levels, boxed notes, figlet banner on first run).

REFERENCE
The Node version uses:
  @clack/prompts  (vertical bar, intro/outro, spinner, note, log.*)
  chalk           (colors, hex)
  figlet          (ASCII banner)
See ghl-agentic-workspace/libs/aw/fmt.mjs in the dev tree for the exact
visual we are matching.

PYTHON STACK (mandatory)
  rich         — colors, panels, spinners, progress, tracebacks
  questionary  — interactive prompts (select/confirm/text)
  pyfiglet     — banner only (lazy-imported)
Do not introduce any other formatting/log libraries. No `logging`, no `loguru`,
no `structlog`. The console helper IS the logger for CLI mode.

GOAL
Create exactly one module — src/mfaw/console.py — that every other file imports
from. After this lands, no other file may call print(), rich.print(), or
construct a Console() instance directly. Grep gate enforced in CI.

API (implement exactly this surface)

  # Framing
  intro(msg: str) -> None              # bold pill, brand color, top bar
  outro(msg: str) -> None               # green, bottom bar
  banner(text: str, subtitle: str = "") -> None   # figlet + dividers, one-shot

  # Logs (each prints with a left-side vertical bar + symbol)
  info(msg: str) -> None      # cyan ◆
  success(msg: str) -> None   # green ◆
  warn(msg: str) -> None      # yellow ▲
  error(msg: str) -> None     # red ■
  step(msg: str) -> None      # magenta ◇

  # Multi-line boxed callout
  note(body: str, title: str | None = None) -> None

  # Spinner — context manager
  spinner(message: str) -> ContextManager[Spinner]
      with spinner("Doing thing") as s:
          s.message("phase 2")
          ...
      # auto-stop on exit; stop("Done") if explicit success message wanted

  # Prompts (thin wrappers over questionary, but rendered through rich theme)
  select(message: str, choices: list[str], default: str | None = None) -> str
  confirm(message: str, default: bool = False) -> bool
  text(message: str, default: str = "") -> str
  # All raise CancelError on Ctrl-C; never return None.

  # Silent + non-TTY
  set_silent(v: bool) -> None
      # When True: all framing/logs/spinners become no-ops. Errors still print.
  is_tty() -> bool
      # False under pytest, CI, pipes. In that mode:
      #   - drop colors
      #   - replace spinners with one-line "… done." after the block
      #   - log lines become plain "INFO: ..." prefixed text

  # MCP-server mode (CRITICAL)
  set_mcp_mode(v: bool) -> None
      # When True: ALL output goes to stderr, never stdout.
      # stdout is reserved for JSON-RPC. Violating this breaks MCP transport.

  # Errors
  class CancelError(Exception): ...   # raised by prompts on Ctrl-C

