ENVIRONMENT HONORING (MUST)
  NO_COLOR=1     → disable all color (rich already honors this; verify)
  CI=true        → set is_tty() to False
  MFAW_SILENT=1  → set_silent(True) at import time
  MFAW_MODE=mcp  → set_mcp_mode(True) at import time
                   (also auto-detected if stdin is not a TTY AND parent
                    process name suggests claude/cursor — but env wins)

IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
- Single module-level Console instance for stdout, single for stderr.
  Switch which is "active" based on mcp_mode.
- Spinner: use rich.progress.Progress with SpinnerColumn + TextColumn,
  transient=True, so it disappears on stop. On non-TTY, print a single
  "… <message>" line on enter and "✓ <stop_message>" on exit.
- Width: read shutil.get_terminal_size().columns; cap at 100 for readability.
- All public functions are sync. No async.

DELIVERABLES
1. src/mfaw/console.py (the only new source file).
2. tests/test_console.py covering:
     - silent mode swallows output
     - non-TTY (capsys) drops colors and spinner becomes inline
     - mcp mode writes nothing to stdout (use capsys)
     - CancelError raised when questionary returns None
3. A grep-based CI check (scripts/check_console_usage.sh) that fails the
   build if any file under src/mfaw/ (excluding console.py itself) contains:
       \bprint\(   |   rich\.print   |   Console\(   |   sys\.stdout\.write
4. Migrate existing CLI command files to import from console. One commit
   per command file (sync, init, doctor, use, status, nuke). Show me diffs
   between commits.
5. README.md: add a 10-line "Console output" section showing a screenshot/
   asciicast of the new look.

ACCEPTANCE
- `mfaw init` shows: banner → intro → 3 step lines → spinner → success → outro
  on a TTY. Same content as plain prefixed text on CI.
- `MFAW_MODE=mcp mfaw status` writes zero bytes to stdout, all to stderr.
- `mfaw --silent sync` shows exactly one line: "Initializing..." and exits.
- Grep gate passes; pytest passes; coverage on console.py > 90%.

OUT OF SCOPE
